  207: #  ---------------------------------------------------------------- triggers
  208: #
  209: #  *** THE FIRST VERSION OF THESE ROWS WAS INVERTED, AND A MEASURING SEAT
  210: #  CAUGHT IT BEFORE ANY CODE WAS WRITTEN. ***
  211: #
  212: #  They asserted that the old fatal() TEXT MUST BE ABSENT.  But the fix this
  213: #  round has agreed -- the #447/#459 shape -- KEEPS the diagnostic and drops
  214: #  only the exit(1).  So the old rows PUNISHED THE INTENDED FIX AND REWARDED
  215: #  DELETING THE REGISTER ARM.  Measured across six builds: the arm replaced by
  216: #  `odata = 0xffff; break;` scored 13/13, while the real fix scored 8/13.
  217: #
  218: #  Re-pinned in ORACLE-CORRECTION ORDER: these expectations are written FIRST
  219: #  and measured RED on the committed build, and only then does the code change.
  220: #  Same scripts, opposite colour -- without that red, a re-pin is indistinguish-
  221: #  able from fitting the test to the binary.
  222: #
  223: #  THE SHAPE THAT DISCRIMINATES: drive the SAME site TWICE in ONE session.
  224: #    pre-fix        -> DIES on the first access                     (red)
  225: #    correct fix    -> survives, diagnostic appears EXACTLY ONCE    (green)
  226: #    deleted arm    -> survives, diagnostic appears ZERO times      (red)
