The diagnostic-count premise holds, with **N = 1**: NODATA has its own once-only latch. I also found a qualification to the event proposal: the scripts describe GD-ROM pending status as sticky, so a bit already set by command dispatch cannot prove that the final read raised a new completion.
exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command '$gdromLine = 0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '"'GXEMUL-SEC\\regress\\gdrom_decline_probe.py' | ForEach-Object { "'$gdromLine++; if (($gdromLine -ge 1 -and $gdromLine -le 175) -or ($gdromLine -ge 400 -and $gdromLine -le 490)) { '"'{0,5}: {1}' -f "'$gdromLine, $_ } }' in C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL
exec
