Q5 needs a distinction: the two counters are equal after every unsegmented read. If that equality is used literally as the exhaustion predicate, it clears availability on the first halfword and fails `accept d1`. The plausible escape is using the segment counter in place of the buffer offset when comparing against `data_len`.
